Subject: vulkan: gate coopmat bf16 on the bfloat16 extension being present

`device->coopmat_bf16_support` is set from cooperative-matrix properties
alone, and then pushes "VK_KHR_shader_bfloat16" into vkCreateDevice on its
own. A driver that reports BF16 matrix configurations without exposing the
shader extension fails device creation outright:

    survey-llamacpp: vk::PhysicalDevice::createDevice: ErrorExtensionNotPresent
    ERROR: vkDestroyFence: Invalid device [VUID-vkDestroyFence-device-parameter]

and the failure is unsurvivable in-process: the exception unwinds into
teardown of a half-initialized device and the loader aborts. Observed on an
AMD Radeon 760M (RDNA3 iGPU), AMD proprietary driver, Windows 11, whose
device banner states the contradiction plainly (bf16: 0, matrix cores:
KHR_coopmat).

The direct shader-bf16 path is already gated this way upstream (the
`if (bfloat16_support)` push in the extension-enumeration block); this
applies the same gate to the coopmat-derived path. Retired when upstream
gates coopmat_bf16_support on the extension list.
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
index e32dd7a56..a719ebed2 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
@@ -6707,6 +6707,13 @@ static vk_device ggml_vk_get_device(size_t idx) {
             device_extensions.push_back("VK_KHR_cooperative_matrix");
         }
 #if defined(VK_KHR_shader_bfloat16)
+        // A driver can report BF16 cooperative-matrix shapes without exposing
+        // VK_KHR_shader_bfloat16 (AMD proprietary on RDNA3 iGPUs); requesting
+        // the extension then fails vkCreateDevice outright. Gate the coopmat
+        // capability on the extension actually being present.
+        if (!bfloat16_support) {
+            device->coopmat_bf16_support = false;
+        }
         if (device->coopmat_bf16_support) {
             device_extensions.push_back("VK_KHR_shader_bfloat16");
         }
